.TH PRX 1 "" "prx 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
prx \- user-space container and path-translation engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prx
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prx
runs a glibc-based Linux root filesystem as an unprivileged user, without
root, namespaces or ptrace. Paths are translated by an
.B LD_PRELOAD
shim and the guest's dynamic loader and libc are patched at run time.
.PP
.B prx
is a convenience tool, not a security boundary: a program that issues raw
syscalls or is statically linked can bypass the translation layer.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build
Compile the C runtime shim and loader patcher (needs a C compiler). Also
tries to build the optional built-in emulator \fBpemu\fR for this host; if
that fails, a note is printed and the build still succeeds.
.TP
\fBinstall\fR \fINAME\fR \fIFILE|URL\fR [\fB\-\-sha256\fR \fIHEX\fR]
Extract a rootfs archive as container NAME. With
.B \-\-sha256
the archive is verified before extraction; without it a warning is printed.
NAME may contain only letters, digits, \fB.\fR, \fB_\fR and \fB\-\fR and must
not start with \fB\-\fR.
.TP
\fBlogin\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIcommand\fR...]
Start a shell or command inside the container.
.RS
.TP
\fB\-b\fR, \fB\-\-bind\fR \fIPATH\fR | \fIHOST\fR:\fIGUEST\fR
Bind a host path into the guest. GUEST must be an absolute path. Paths must be
shorter than 1024 bytes and must not contain
.B :
or
.BR = ;
at most 50 binds can be given. Invalid binds are rejected with an error.
.TP
\fB\-w\fR, \fB\-\-workdir\fR \fIDIR\fR
Initial working directory inside the guest, as an absolute guest path
(default /root; with \fB\-\-no\-root\-id\fR as a non-root user, the user's home).
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-env\fR \fIKEY=VAL\fR
Pass an environment variable. May be given more than once.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-root\-id
Run as the host user instead of fake root.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-seccomp
Skip the workarounds for a host seccomp policy (Android): the loader/libc patch,
the SIGSYS handler and the GLIBC_TUNABLES rseq default. Same as PRX_SECCOMP=0.
.TP
.B \-\-trace
Debug syscall and seccomp tracing.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; everything after it is the command to run. Unknown options
are an error, so put \fB\-\-\fR before a command that starts with \fB\-\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B list
List installed containers.
.TP
\fBfixperm\fR \fINAME\fR
Repair permissions and flush the library-path cache.
.TP
\fBremove\fR \fINAME\fR
Delete a container and its derived files.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V ", " version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PRX_HOME
Data directory. Default: \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/prx\fR (\fI~/.local/share/prx\fR).
.TP
.B PRX_SRCDIR
Directory containing \fIprx.c\fR, \fIldpatch.c\fR and the \fIshim/\fR modules.
.TP
.B PRX_SECCOMP
0 skips the host-seccomp workarounds, like \fB\-\-no\-seccomp\fR (default 1).
.TP
.B PRX_SHIM_CFLAGS
Extra compiler flags for the shim, for example \fB\-DPRX_NO_SECCOMP\fR. Run \fBprx build\fR afterwards.
.TP
.B CC
C compiler used by \fBprx build\fR.
.TP
.B PRX_QEMU
Path (or command name) of a specific qemu-user binary for cross-architecture rootfs.
.B pemu
selects the built-in experimental emulator installed in \fI$PRX_HOME/lib\fR (see
.BR EMULATOR ).
An i386 rootfs always needs qemu-i386 (there is no native i386 mode).
.TP
.B PRX_DNS
IPv4 and/or IPv6 nameservers to use inside the guest, separated by commas,
semicolons or blanks. Invalid entries and scoped addresses such as
.I fe80::1%eth0
are ignored with a warning.
.TP
.B PRX_KEEP
Set to 1 to leave guest processes running after
.B prx login
exits. By default they are terminated.
.TP
.BR QEMU_CPU ", " QEMU_STRACE ", " QEMU_LOG ", " QEMU_RESERVED_VA ", " QEMU_GUEST_BASE ", " QEMU_PAGESIZE
Passed through to the emulator when one is used.
.TP
.B GLIBC_TUNABLES
Passed to the guest; defaults to \fBglibc.pthread.rseq=0\fR when unset.
.TP
.B PEMU_JIT
Set to 0 to disable the JIT of the built-in emulator (same as \fBpemu \-nojit\fR).
.TP
.B PEMU_JIT_STATS
Set to 1 to print JIT block counts and interpreter fallbacks at exit
(x86_64-guest emulator).
.TP
.B PRX_NO_ARGV0
Set to 1 to never pass
.B \-\-argv0
to the glibc loader. Normally this is detected automatically, because
.B \-\-argv0
exists only in glibc 2.33 and later; with an older rootfs the guest shell sees
its full path as argv[0].
.SH EMULATOR
.B pemu
is a small, experimental user-mode emulator that can replace qemu-user:
an aarch64 rootfs on x86_64 hosts, an x86_64 rootfs on aarch64 hosts. It is
built by \fBprx build\fR and used with \fBPRX_QEMU=pemu prx login\fR NAME.
It has a JIT (disable with \fBPEMU_JIT=0\fR), is much slower than native, and
is not a security boundary. The aarch64-guest emulator has no threads; the
x86_64-guest emulator supports them. Use qemu-user for anything serious.
.SH SECURITY NOTES
Inside the guest, PAM is configured to always succeed and sudo is configured
with NOPASSWD, because there is no real root to authenticate against. Do not
treat the guest as a sandbox for untrusted code.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Only glibc rootfs are supported (not musl). Only x86_64 and aarch64 hosts.
A rootfs of the other architecture runs through qemu-user (or pemu); an i386
rootfs only through qemu-i386, there is no native i386 mode.
The loader patch depends on glibc's machine code and may not apply to every
version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PRX_HOME/rootfs/NAME
Container root filesystems.
.TP
.I $PRX_HOME/lib
Per-user built shim, patched loaders and the optional \fIpemu\fR emulator.
.TP
.I $PRX_HOME/dl
Downloaded rootfs archives.
